# Never publish an app to AmL One without "publish"

**HARD GATE.** Do not put any app on the AmL One store unless **this
conversation** uses the word **publish** and clearly means **that app on
AmL One** (the store / shelf / listing).

Product OTA (`publish MessageMe`, `build the app`) is **not** permission
to list that app on AmL One. A prior chat where they once said publish
does not count.

## Forbidden without that ask

```
❌ Add or restore a row in OFFICIAL_LISTINGS
❌ Deploy AmL One so a new official app appears on Today
❌ POST https://aml.one/api/publish/android (or any store publish API)
❌ Community shelf upload
❌ Listing an app after a sideload, APK build, or listing-copy draft
```

These do **not** authorize a store listing:

```
❌ put it on my phone / 17 Ultra
❌ build the app / build the APK
❌ deploy (servers)
❌ prepare the listing / future listing
```

## Allowed

```
✅ "publish Gallery to the store" / "publish it on AmL One"
✅ Changing copy of an app already on the shelf when they asked to change that copy
✅ The user publishing from the AmL One or App Builder UI themselves
```

Copy this file to every new AmL app as `.cursor/rules/never-store-without-publish.mdc`
with `alwaysApply: true`.
